# text_id = 1583
# text = On the question of individual choice in the ballot box , there is no real difference — especially given the increasingly grand functions that are conferred in the European arena — between what is decided in the House of Commons and what is decided in the European institutions , which are increasingly seen as a superior sphere of law .
