# text_id = 1591
# text = Someone from England , Wales or Northern Ireland — especially Northern Ireland , which lacks enough universities , and which sends many students to Scotland — will , absurdly , have to pay £ 4,000 in tuition fees to follow a four - year course in a Scottish university , whereas a Scottish student will have to pay only £ 3,000 .
