# text = As my hon . Friend the Member for Poole ( Mr. Syms ) said , an individual pensioner living on a fixed income will be discriminated against when he has set his arrangements for retirement on the basis of certain knowledge that the current UK tax rate will be the contribution tax relief and the basis on which he is taxed .
