# text_id = 1743
# text = Scottish law is more reasonable in that respect and is geared to preserve what was formerly a feature of English law ; namely , that the estate of the deceased was divided into three parts , one being the widow 's part , the second being the bairns ' part and only the third part being subject to testamentary disposition .
