# text_id = 1786
# text = A recent study by the crime prevention unit suggests that improved street lighting cannot be shown directly to reduce crime , although that does not , of course , mean that it is not a useful aspect of a more general programme of crime reduction , as has been shown to be the case in the refurbishment of certain estates in London where crime figures have been particularly high .
