# text_id = 1842
# text = Violence has characterised the relations between Britain and Ireland over many years , and many of us have sat in this House when anti-terrorist legislation has been introduced , yet the only gain there has ever been was when this Government had the wisdom to open negotiations with the nationalists , which made possible the Belfast agreement , the referendum , the Assembly and the prospect of peace in the future .
