# text_id = 1893
# text = For 30 years , British public spending has been characterised by the annual spending round rather than long - term planning ; by the year - to - year bidding culture , with all the problems of hurried end - of - year corrections , instead of the strategic planning of resources ; by incremental bids that are not tied to outcomes , rather than spending to achieve defined results .
