# text_id = 1922
# text = Government Amendments Nos. 88A , 89A , 89B and 89C are consequential to the new power to require the giving of security by third parties under Clause 38 , and are designed to clarify that a person who has given security on behalf of a detainee may inform an immigration officer or constable of his belief that a person bailed is about to abscond , thus leading to arrest without warrant .
