# text_id = 1937
# text = Fifty years ago , back in 1947 , the report on possible national parks drawn up by the Hobhouse committee for the post - war Labour Government identified the south downs for inclusion in the national parks programme , but , when the national parks were being designated in the 1950s , under the National Parks and Access to the Countryside Act 1949 , the south downs were left out .
